Looking at the jagged edges: the wavy top of D fits exactly the curved right side of E (shown in matching color), the right side of A fits the right side of D, the top of A fits the top of C, and the right side of C fits the top of E. These four pieces (A, C, D, E) pair up perfectly along all four internal seams to form the square with straight sides outside.

Piece B, however, has a right edge (highlighted in blue) that matches none of the other pieces' edges, so B cannot be fitted into the square.

\boxed{B}
